<metadata><name>Frissell Point</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:246-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.205572" lon="-122.039668"><ele>523.6</ele><name>Road 2650 at Highway 126</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:frissell-road-2650 (OSM node 40277666); confidence: high; pdf_page: 248; book_elev_ft: 1600; quote: Road 2650, the ski route, starts at Highway 126 2.5 miles north of the Highway 126/242 junction ... Starting at 1,600 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.204699" lon="-122.060273"><ele>838.4</ele><name>Road 613 junction</name><desc>source: USFS EDW start of road 2650613 on 2650; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 248; book_elev_ft: 3000; quote: At 3,000 feet, 3.2 miles from the highway, you will encounter two side roads ... Road 613 ... Just beyond, Road 620</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.218300" lon="-122.103900"><ele>1504.6</ele><name>Road 2650 end, north of Frissell Point</name><desc>source: end of OSM way 1019268594 (Forest Road 2650), 0.45 mi north of OSM peak node 7881593252 Frissell Point; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 248; quote: Another 3.2 miles takes you to a junction north of the peak where a road goes north along the long, narrow ridgecrest.</desc></wpt>
